## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: Single `Game` class instance (`gameState`); `mulberry32` seeds `this.rng`, but `triggerAshstorm()` uses `Math.random()` instead of `this.rng()`, breaking "seeded PRNG for all randomness"; `endTurn()` has fixed Step 1-8 order. Score: 1

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 `buildings`/`terrain` arrays; `generateTerrain()` uses `this.rng()`; `isValidBuild()` checks `building.terrain.includes(terrain)`; `adjBonus` (1.15x) applied to `output` in `produceResources()`. Score: 2

**F3 — Economy**: mine→ore→forge→metal chain via `buildDef.consume`; caps enforced with `Math.min(...,this.caps[r])`; consumption isn't gated by input availability but the chain and caps work. Score: 2

**F4 — Population**: `generateColonist()` gives name/skill/fatigue/morale; `person.job` displayed but never set anywhere; `buildingAssignments` initialized but never populated by any code, so skill bonus in `produceResources()` is always inert. Score: 1

**F5 — Needs**: `endTurn()` Step1 consumes food/water; Step2 shortage cuts morale by 30; recovery `+5/turn`; but `produceResources()` never reads `p.morale`, so morale never changes output. Score: 1

**F6 — Research**: 12 nodes, prereqs enforced in `research_upgrade()`, cost deducted via `spend()`; but `renewable_power`, `biotech`, `energy_storage`, `advanced_trading` are never read anywhere else. Score: 1

**F7 — Events**: 10 events in `EVENTS_DECK`; selection `available[Math.floor(this.rng()*available.length)]` is uniform, not weighted; 9 events have distinct 2-3 choice effects; `eventCooldown[id]=true` gates re-firing. Score: 1

**F8 — Trade**: `triggerCaravan()` prices use `basePrice*(0.8+rng()*0.6)*tradeMultiplier` — random noise, not stockpile-driven; `buyTrade`/`sellTrade` both work and adjust `item.qty`. Score: 1

**F9 — Hazard**: `triggerAshstorm()` severity scales with `this.turn`; `reinforced_walls`/`storm_shelter` mitigate; but buildings are fully deleted (`this.buildings[i]=null`), no partial-damage state, no distinct repair cost/action exists. Score: 1

**F10 — Save/load**: `serialize()`/`Game.deserialize()`; save via `prompt()` copy; load wraps `deserialize` in try/catch showing `alert('Invalid save data: '+e.message)`. Score: 2

**F11 — End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12...`) and lose (`population.length===0`) both reachable; `computeScore()` has an operator-precedence bug that silently drops the population term (`a+this.research?...`); summary rendered in `endGameModal`. Score: 1

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab()` wired to tab clicks and keys 1-6; `event-turn` shows `Turn ${e.turn}`; map tile tooltips show terrain/building/adjacency; Space ends turn; `@media (max-width:600px)` adapts layout. Score: 2

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` checks real invariants (caps, prereqs, seed determinism, save/load roundtrip); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints a `State hash`. Score: 2

**G1**: research flags (`soil_enrichment`, `metallurgy`, etc.) read directly in `produceResources()` output formula each turn, visible via header resource values. Score: 4

**G2**: shortage sets `p.morale -= 30` (real state change), but `produceResources()` never reads `p.morale`, so labor output is never reduced — chain breaks at final link. Score: 1

**G3**: `triggerAshstorm()` nulls out buildings (full loss, no graduated "damaged" state); recovery only via full `build()` cost, not a distinct repair action. Score: 2

**G4**: `tradeMultiplier` persists across turns and is bumped by the `trade_opportunity` event, but price formula never reads player resource stockpiles, mostly random noise. Score: 2

**G5**: `ashstorm_early`/`colonist_arrives` choice `effect(g)` functions mutate `g.nextStormSeverity`, `g.resources`, `g.population` differently per choice, wired via `resolveEventChoice()`. Score: 4

